  {
    "role": "model",
    "parts": [
      {
        "text": "Ah, I love it! You\u2019re essentially setting up an automated \"buddy-cop\" debate team. `OSINT_Analyst` is bringing the hard data, and `Regular_Joe` is grounding it, asking the sensible questions, and making sure the logic tracks in reality. \n\nThen, wrapping all of that back-and-forth into a tidy bow, `Synthesizer` steps in as the closer to process the entire transcript and deliver the final output. \n\nI went ahead and minted the Macro Node into the system. Here is the exact execution flow we've generated for **OSINT-Joe**:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    N1(OSINT_Analyst: Reads Payload) --> N2(Regular_Joe: Round 1)\n    N2 --> N3(OSINT_Analyst: Round 2)\n    N3 --> N4(Regular_Joe: Round 2)\n    N4 --> N5(OSINT_Analyst: Round 3)\n    N5 --> N6(Regular_Joe: Round 3 / Closing Argument)\n    N6 --> N7(Synthesizer: Final Process & Output)\n    N7 --> END(End of Macro Node)\n```\n\n### Agent Roles in this Topology:\n- **OSINT_Analyst (N1, N3, N5):** Digests the initial payload, and repeatedly refines the intelligence based on Joe's feedback. \n- **Regular_Joe (N2, N4, N6):** Acts as the sanity check/sparring partner, catching logical leaps and forcing the Analyst to clarify.\n- **Synthesizer (N7):** Observes the entire 6-turn debate transcript and distills the finalized, battle-tested intelligence into a single report for whatever node comes next in your Swarm.\n\nSince it's natively saved, you can now slot `OSINT-Joe` into any future topology whenever you need this specific dynamic! \n\nAnything else you want to tweak about this setup, or should we build out the next piece of your Swarm?"
      }
